  "notes": "きっちり emphasizes precision and leaving no room for error or gaps. It conveys thoroughness and meticulousness.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- きっちり{時間|じかん}を{守|まも}る: keep time precisely\n- きっちり{払|はら}う: pay the exact amount\n- きっちり{閉|し}める: shut tightly\n- きっちりした{人|ひと}: a meticulous person (na-adjective use)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- きちんと: properly, neatly (broader — about doing things the right way)\n- ぴったり: exactly, perfectly fitting (often for size or match)\n- きっかり: exactly, precisely (numbers and time only)\n- ちゃんと: properly (more casual, often used with children)\n\nREGISTER:\nNeutral. Used in both spoken and written Japanese.",
